WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.135
Right now, we're following new warnings

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.003
from Washington

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:03.970
to Beijing

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.672
about the Chinese spy balloon now

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.374
flying over the United States.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:07.741
U.S.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.042
officials are not ruling out

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.977
the possibility of shooting down

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:11.945
the balloon.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.513
Brian Todd is working the story for us.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.748
Brian, what are you learning about

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.383
spy balloons like this one

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.684
and how they actually work?

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.385
Wolf, analysts

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:20.053
say spy balloons have been used in war

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:22.122
as far back as the 1700s

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.790
through the American Civil War

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.524
and up to the wars

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.226
in Iraq and Afghanistan.

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:26.793
Experts say

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.094
they may look unwieldy,

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.330
but don't let that fool you

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.198
This is floating there.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.300
That's what's the weirdest part about it.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.302
That tiny white dot in the sky

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.804
can seem deceptive.

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:38.705
This suspected

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.073
Chinese spy balloon

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:41.608
experts say, is a vehicle

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:42.709
that's more impressive

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:43.877
than you might think.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.745
Balloons have a long history in warfare

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:46.212
being used

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:46.846
for intelligence,

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:47.947
surveillance, reconnaissance.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.682
And this is no different U.S.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.117
officials say this balloon

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.186
now moving over the central U.S.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.288
is the size of three city busses

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:55.922
and appears

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.390
to have solar panels on it,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.659
as well as surveillance equipment.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.561
Analysts say since the balloon likely

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.695
has no motor,

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.963
the solar panels would help

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.031
power the balloon

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:08.268
and to allow for an operator

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.371
to steer the balloon because any steering

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.572
mechanism would require

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.574
some degree of power as well.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.208
Experts say

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.376
these balloons can fly

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:19.512
at altitudes of 60,000 feet to 50 miles

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.580
above the earth.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.714
We asked analysts

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.349
what kind of surveillance equipment

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.684
this vehicle might have

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.820
and the capabilities of that equipment.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.887
They'll have cameras

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.023
for imagery of sensitive sites.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.324
They can have other sensors

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.059
that can collect signals intelligence.

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:34.227
So think about

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.429
eavesdropping on your cell phone.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.363
These are these buildings

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.765
have been around for a long time.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.666
And we ourselves in

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:40.767
the United States have used them

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.902
simply to monitor

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.971
the ground in Iraq and Afghanistan.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.906
But with military satellites

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:47.941
having such sophistic

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.742
cated surveillance capability,

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.077
what would a spy balloon

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.946
have that a satellite wouldn't?

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.714
One, they fly at lower altitudes.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:55.748
And the other big advantage

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:56.549
I think they have

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.450
is the persistence

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.318
they can just kind of

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.420
hang out and loiter over sites,

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.387
whereas satellites,

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:02.856
of course, are in low-Earth

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.657
orbit, are rotating around the earth.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:05.792
And experts say

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.227
balloons are much cheaper

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.995
to deploy than satellites.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:11.264
But the spy balloon, as possibly evidence

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.266
in this case, isn't infallible.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.168
One of their biggest drawbacks

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:15.835
historically is

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:16.870
that they can just get carried

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.704
away by the wind.

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:18.872
We tried to use them

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.206
to spy on the Soviet Union

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.007
during the Cold War,

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.509
and that was our big problem.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.210
So if it's not shot down,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.745
how would a balloon like this

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:27.046
eventually come down?

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:27.981
Would it just be allowed

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.382
to crash somewhere

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.384
if they steer them properly?

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.219
They can just like you would

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:33.853
in a hot air

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.422
balloon over Santa Fe, New Mexico.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.491
They would bring that down

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:41.161
in a very controlled descent.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:42.962
Experts say

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:43.730
the spy balloon

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.533
has a future and possibly an ominous one.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.168
They say it could be used

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.702
as a weapons platform,

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:51.304
possibly to attack cities

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.139
or static formations of troops.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.340
As one analyst said,

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.074
there's no limit

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.142
to the kind of technology

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:56.910
you can stick

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.878
on the bottom of a balloon Wolf.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:02:59.312
Look forward.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.014
And warfare maybe in the future.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:01.714
We'll see what happens.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.882
Brian, thank you very much

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:03.550
for that report.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.618
I want to bring in CNN's Fareed Zakaria

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:06.219
right now.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.421
He's the host of Fareed Zakaria GPS.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.023
Fareed, thanks for joining us.

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:10.823
As you know,

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:11.324
White House

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:12.325
officials have viewed

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.693
U.s.-china relations

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.895
as improving, following President Biden's

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:16.729
November

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.298
meeting with the Chinese president

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:19.465
Xi Jinping.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.234
How has the presidents of this spy

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:24.504
balloon abruptly seemingly changed that

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:26.773
Well,

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:29.542
it points to the central dynamic

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.878
between the US-China relations,

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.080
which is domestic politics.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.749
Look, the whole spy balloon aspect

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.451
reminds me of that,

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:41.454
that a scene in Casablanca, you know,

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.189
I'll be really that shocked

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.692
that the Chinese are spying on us.

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:48.061
We spy on the Chinese every day.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:50.964
The Chinese have very sophisticated

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.065
military satellites

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:53.499
that spy on us all the time.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.468
They're spy planes that do so.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.270
I myself doubt very much

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.838
that this is as sophisticated

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.573
as people are saying. If it was.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:01.474
Why the hell did it

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:02.542
veer off course

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:05.044
so dramatically as it did here?

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.713
There is very little as far

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:07.580
the intelligence people

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.449
I've talked to don't believe that

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.451
there is much additional capacity.

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:12.285
Again,

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.454
this is as as your report pointed out,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.555
something that was used

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:16.756
in the French Revolution.

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:17.991
This is not exactly cutting

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:19.158
edge technology.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.293
But more importantly,

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.828
of course, the Chinese spy on us.

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:23.162
We spy on them.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:25.331
The purpose of Anthony Blinken's

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:29.102
visit to China was precisely to stabilize

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.871
a difficult relationship,

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:33.840
a competitive relationship.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.809
The reason we have relations with other

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:39.178
great powers is not as a gift to them.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:41.080
It's to secure our interests,

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.248
to preserve the peace,

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.950
to preserve stability

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.251
I don't understand

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:47.220
the purpose of canceling the trip,

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.622
the presence of a spy balloon,

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.523
let us assume it is.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.859
That is even more

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.894
reason to have a conversation with them,

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:56.296
to figure out what guardrails

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:56.796
we can have

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.998
for a very difficult relationship.

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:01.100
So you think Secretary of State Blinken

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.269
made a major blunder in canceling

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:03.970
that trip?

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:06.372
I think

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.308
Secretary Blinken and the administration

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:09.876
are not reacting to China.

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:12.045
They are reacting to Kevin McCarthy

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:14.747
and Marco Rubio and Ted Cruz,

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.885
who have all used this as a as a way

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.753
to attack the administration.

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:21.721
Donald Trump is saying

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.889
shoot down the balloon.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:25.191
So you have, you know,

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.626
basically a bunch of people on the right

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.661
who want to go to war because

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.730
because the Chinese

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:31.898
because they have suddenly discovered

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.800
that China spies on us

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.669
and the administration feels compelled to

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.805
in some way seem tough.

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:40.273
It's a very bad dynamic

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:42.041
because it fundamentally

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.109
stops as you said,

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:44.010
the whole point

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.012
was to try to have some kind

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:48.014
of serious conversation with the Chinese

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.148
about the many issues

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.584
on which we have serious disagreements

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:52.485
and problems.

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:53.986
I mean, we met with the Soviet Union

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:54.587
all the time.

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:56.622
It's you know, they were spying on us

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:57.990
throughout the Cold War.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.559
We still met with them.

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:01.194
So what should the US response

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:02.695
to this balloon flying over

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:03.863
the United States have been

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:06.132
I think

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:07.066
Blinken should have gone

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:07.967
that disgusted

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.369
with them, talked about

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:13.439
we need a lot more arms control measures

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:14.374
with the Chinese.

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:17.543
We have a lot of procedures with

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.846
Russia still there, holdover

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:20.880
from the Cold War.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.180
You know,

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.550
we we have the arms control treaties.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.085
We have confidence building measures.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:28.488
We have a hotline between Moscow

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:30.790
and Washington all to make sure

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.726
there aren't accidental events like this.

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.762
There is a miscalculation

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:36.863
because remember, China

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:38.297
also is a nuclear power.

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:39.399
It has intercontinental

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:40.433
ballistic missiles.

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:42.268
It has nuclear weapons.

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:44.337
And we want to stabilize

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:45.004
the relationship.

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:45.872
We want to make sure

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:47.440
that nobody is miscalculating.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.475
So it feels to me like

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:51.477
that's all the more reason to go

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:54.213
and have serious conversations with them.

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:54.647
You know,

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:55.581
when I'm talking to them

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:57.116
as a gift to them

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.651
for some kind of good behavior,

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.352
we're talking to them

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:00.520
because they're the second

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.488
largest economy in the world.

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:04.891
And essentially the other

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:07.326
burgeoning superpower in the world.

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.728
Fareed Zakaria, as usual,

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:10.296
thank you very much for joining us in.

